# SFT execution status v0.107

2026-09-23. Full-size control binding and a private one-shot worker-call adapter
are implemented and locally tested. Pure guard-side plan/mount inventory
binding is also implemented. **Native guardian integration and Gate 5 are not
complete.** No S3 transfer, model import, remote action or GPU execution occurred.

## Completed code

- `posttraining_checkpoint_fullsize_entry_v1.py` binds the exact eight control
  bodies, entry/source/attempt pins and runtime-source bytes, reuses the frozen
  resource validators, and provides a private fixed-path coordinator adapter.
  Once a coordinator call starts, success, failure or malformed returned evidence
  consumes that worker-process attempt. Returned evidence is limited to a
  bounded digest and allowlisted scalars.
- `posttraining_checkpoint_fullsize_guard_v1.py` binds the exact plan inventories
  to the existing mount validator and derives proposed memory/deadline limits
  from the envelope. It does not install these limits, start a clock, prove
  supplied host identities or implement the native guardian lifecycle.

Both new public APIs still immediately reject `host_guard_not_bound`.
The private adapter is only a future independently admitted guardian target;
all local calls used runtime/coordinator doubles. Hashes bind supplied bytes,
not origin, permission, input immutability or host admission.

## Verification

All **249 unique tests passed on both CPython 3.11.15 and 3.13.7**:
32 new entry tests, 16 new guard tests and 201 unchanged regression tests.
The generated full-size metadata case describes 4,002,376,704 parameters with
a 64 GiB worker proposal and 3,600-second deadline. It performs integer-only
planning, not tensor allocation or actual checkpoint conversion.

Ruff passed for all four new source/test files. A fresh isolated import loaded
no ML modules and confirmed both public calls reject. Independent review
confirmed the scoped control bindings, fixed paths, consumed-attempt behavior
and honest execution boundary.

All 21 existing readiness bindings and 78 qualified native source hashes
remain unchanged. Tracked and staged diffs are empty; these additions and
other pre-existing untracked work remain local. The new sources have not been
added to the frozen native qualification manifest or remotely qualified.

