## Next actual work

Implement the full-size native guardian/controller/bootstrap lifecycle with
independent PID/cgroup supervision and hard timeout, testing it locally with
syscall doubles first. Resolve cumulative native-write enforcement and
separately bounded setup, OS, scratch and report writes before enabling real
execution. Existing cooperative content reservations and filesystem capacity
do not prove those writes are cumulatively enforced.

The existing host/runtime/source admission, immutable backing or writer
exclusion, mount/resource readback and combined execution/transfer approval
requirements remain open. No new policy gate is introduced here, and the old
eight-field host contract is unchanged. A real import must wait for those
premises and its exact authorization; training and production remain disabled.

The previously bound pretrained base remains the S3-backed checkpoint recorded
in v0.106; current S3 availability was not rechecked. No GPU needs to be turned
on for the next local implementation work.
